description:
To enable Blackburn with Darwen Borough Council to fulfil their statutory duty the Contractor is to undertake Captive Shot Blasting Retexturing and Crack Sealing works to support the Council&#039;s Capital Programme.

The Contractor is to undertake site assessments taking into consideration the category and condition of the Highway to assess for suitability before any works are planned or carried out.

The works will encompass the following:
- Captive Shot Blasting Retexturing;
- Fill and Overband Crack Sealing to SHW Clause 711;
- Replacement of Road Markings;
- Liaison with Stakeholders and the Public;
- Traffic Management

This Scheme will cover the resurfacing of highways on:
•	Wycollar Road, Blackburn
•	Billinge Close, Blackburn
•	St James Road, Blackburn
•	Old Bank Lane, Blackburn
•	Lynwood Avenue, Darwen
•	Birch Hall Avenue, Darwen

And will encompass the following works:
•	Carriageway inlay resurfacing;
•	Reconstruction of speed tables/humps
•	Adjustment and/or replacement of ironwork;
•	Replacement of road markings;
•	Replacement of pedestrian delineation studs;
•	Liaison with stakeholders and the public;
•	Traffic management.

This Scheme will cover the Surface Dressing of highways on:
•	Bolton Road, Edgworth;
•	Bury Road, Edgworth;
•	East Park Road, Blackburn;
•	Heys Lane, Blackburn;
•	Livesey Branch Road, Blackburn;
•	Long Lane, Blackburn;
•	Shadsworth Road; Blackburn;
•	Stones Bank Road; West Pennine

And will encompass the following works:
•	Acting as Principal Contractor;
